fix: volume permissions on Railway (SQLite "unable to open database file")

Railway mounts volumes AFTER the image is built, which replaces /app/data with
a root-owned mount. The Dockerfile's build-time chown cannot apply to a mount
that does not exist yet, so the unprivileged 'marquee' user had no write access
and aiosqlite failed to create the database.

Add a docker-entrypoint.sh that runs as root, ensures DATA_DIR exists and is
owned by 'marquee', then drops privileges via su-exec before exec'ing the app.

Also add .gitattributes pinning *.sh to LF. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel
look for "/bin/sh\r" and fail with a misleading "no such file or directory".
